  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Action and handing over",
     "texto": [
      "**V-아/어다(가) 주다** presents an action whose result or object is taken to another place to hand it over to someone. It is used with verbs that allow that movement: **사다 주다** (to buy and bring/give), **가져다 주다** (to take and hand over). After another action, 가 is often left out.",
      "도서관에서 책을 **빌려다 줬어요** = I borrowed the book at the library and brought it to you."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Not to be confused with -아/어 주다",
     "texto": [
      "**V-아/어 주다** expresses doing something for another person. **V-아/어다 주다** adds the route or transfer of the result to the recipient. **사다 주세요** usually asks for it to be bought and taken to the recipient; **사 주세요** asks for it to be bought as a favour, without stressing the transfer. The context makes the destination clear.",
      "커피를 **사다 주세요** = please buy me the coffee and bring it to me."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "Action",
     "columnas": [
